# The projection is deliberately slowed down by 2 s (appsettings.json → Projections:DelayMs)
# so that the read side can be seen "lagging" behind the write side. Set 0 to make it almost immediate.
@base = http://localhost:5108
@alice = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@bob = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222

### [Query] Alice's statement: balance, number of operations, 5 latest operations (ready-to-use view)
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}

### [Command] Withdraw 100 € → 202 Accepted (nothing to return)
POST {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}/withdrawal
Content-Type: application/json

{ "amount": 100 }

### [Query] Alice's statement IMMEDIATELY after: still the old balance (projection not done yet)
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{alice}}

### [Observability] Projection lag (run again: the lag drops back to 0 after 2 s)
GET {{base}}/admin/projections

### [Command] Transfer from Alice to Bob
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "{{bob}}", "amount": 250 }

### [Command] Rejected by the pipeline validation, before even reaching the handler (400)
POST {{base}}/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "{{alice}}", "amount": 9000 }

### [Query] Bob's paginated history
GET {{base}}/accounts/{{bob}}/operations?page=1&size=10

### [Query] Dashboard: maintained by the projection, never recomputed
GET {{base}}/dashboard
